{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"d704e1662179099e","type":"group","x":2270,"y":865,"width":400,"height":395,"label":"Labels (from lidar, never an input)","color":"3"},
		{"id":"62ad40ed1d6b2a0b","type":"group","x":2270,"y":-70,"width":400,"height":895,"label":"Head input x: 68 channels in this run","color":"4"},
		{"id":"932dba2f266f7efb","type":"group","x":1790,"y":-70,"width":400,"height":1330,"label":"Load time (ConfidenceDataset, per run)"},
		{"id":"cc9483b2fd3c5429","type":"group","x":1310,"y":-70,"width":400,"height":1330,"label":"confcache entry (nuscenes-trainval)","color":"5"},
		{"id":"52dcc8345d392837","type":"group","x":450,"y":-70,"width":780,"height":1330,"label":"Cache build (once per image, same for every run)"},
		{"id":"3f21c934af52f9ef","type":"group","x":-30,"y":-70,"width":400,"height":1330,"label":"nuScenes (raw data)"},
		{"id":"21a693abf9e3eab3","type":"text","text":"# `run1`\n\nNothing. This is the first training run on the full trainval cache, with every input on.\n\n**On:** decoder features (64), depth (1), temporal spread (1), radar (2)\n\n**Head input:** 68 channels","x":0,"y":-520,"width":860,"height":380},
		{"id":"931cb642965dc177","type":"text","text":"## Question\n\nDoes the head learn at all on the full trainval cache with every input?\n\n**Flags added to the default config:** none (the default `configs/train-trainval.toml`)\n\n**Checkpoint:** `nadayusc/confhead/run1` on Hugging Face","x":920,"y":-520,"width":800,"height":380},
		{"id":"292c924f60d08bf5","type":"text","text":"## Result\n\nBest dev loss **0.5562**. `run-v1-radar` repeats this run with the same settings and lands at 0.5566. The gap of 0.0004 between the two is the only measure of repeat noise the team has, so a gap below about 0.001 between any two runs is a tie.\n\nDev loss only shows that a run learned. The Eval team's AUSE and AURG on the val split decide which run is best.","x":1780,"y":-520,"width":860,"height":380},
		{"id":"3bbc4ed2f42a1d72","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n\nRead left to right: raw data, cache build, cache, load time, head.\n\n- Orange: raw nuScenes data\n- Purple: a computation\n- Cyan: an array stored in the confcache\n- Green: a channel the head reads in this run\n- Red: switched off, or changed, in this run\n- Yellow: labels and output\n\nCompare with the baseline: [[run-v1-radar.canvas|run-v1-radar]]","x":2700,"y":-520,"width":880,"height":380},
		{"id":"c93cd9b6cc7bd490","type":"text","text":"**Camera keyframe image**\n\n`[3, 900, 1600]`\n\nOne of 6 cameras.","x":0,"y":0,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"820666e9d89197df","type":"text","text":"**Neighbor frames and camera poses**\n\nFrames at offsets -2, -1, +1, +2 (12 Hz)","x":0,"y":340,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"f4b6781b56169d9b","type":"text","text":"**Radar points**\n\n5 radars, the last 5 sweeps each, about 94 points per image.\n\nDepth in meters, but no elevation.","x":0,"y":510,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0e87894896dd4352","type":"text","text":"**Lidar points**\n\nDepth in meters. The ground truth: it makes the labels and is never an input of the head.","x":0,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0f41814dbad82f77","type":"text","text":"**Frozen Depth Anything V2 (ViT-B)**\n\nDINOv2 encoder, then DPT decoder, on the image resized to 924 x 518.\n\nNever trained here.","x":480,"y":0,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"98d7ee1e4589aac3","type":"text","text":"**Tap `output_conv1`**\n\nLast decoder feature map, 64 channels. Area-averaged to the grid.","x":860,"y":0,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b16eaed506cc06a2","type":"text","text":"**Disparity output**\n\nRelative inverse depth, no units. Area-averaged to the grid.","x":860,"y":170,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"872151ed741814e9","type":"text","text":"**DA2 on the 4 neighbor frames**\n\n4 extra passes per image","x":480,"y":340,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d836e9eceb0e88e1","type":"text","text":"**`temporal_variation`**\n\nFollow each cell's 3D point into the neighbors; std / mean of its inverse depth across frames.","x":860,"y":340,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"bfd6ed2aa342898d","type":"text","text":"**Project radar into the camera**\n\nEach point becomes (u, v, z) and takes DA2's disparity at its pixel.","x":480,"y":510,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a7a6ffc72a979ca8","type":"text","text":"**Radar fit**\n\nFits DA2's disparity to the radar points using least squares fit (see info block below for more info)","x":860,"y":510,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"502182049aef03dd","type":"text","text":"**Project lidar into the camera**\n\nEach point becomes (u, v, z) and takes DA2's disparity at its pixel.","x":480,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7dd298ac46a3d864","type":"text","text":"**Lidar fit**\n\nFits DA2's disparity to the lidar points using least squares fit (see info block below for more info)","x":860,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ae5d25f2fce6faa8","type":"text","text":"`features`\n\n`[64, 74, 132]` float16","x":1340,"y":0,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"8eba18f11352f468","type":"text","text":"`disparity_grid`\n\n`[74, 132]` float32","x":1340,"y":170,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6afca8cbbd4b7bb8","type":"text","text":"`temporal_relstd`\n\n`[74, 132]` float16","x":1340,"y":340,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d4afd09e2cdd9bbe","type":"text","text":"`radar`\n\n`[N, 6]`: u, v, z, dt, sweep, disparity","x":1340,"y":510,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d4037daa3b157767","type":"text","text":"`meta.fit_radar`\n\nscale, shift","x":1340,"y":680,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"4a7a81197ccbc03f","type":"text","text":"`lidar`\n\n`[N, 6]`: u, v, z, dt, sweep, disparity","x":1340,"y":900,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"231ddbd0befac562","type":"text","text":"`meta.fit_lidar`\n\nscale, shift","x":1340,"y":1070,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"d4259240c326c69f","type":"text","text":"**`normalized_disparity`**\n\nDisparity over its image mean. No fit, no meters.","x":1820,"y":170,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5c649c9ec0b22c26","type":"text","text":"**`radar_channels`**\n\nAt each radar point: |fitted depth - z| / z.\n\nEach point fills 3 x 3 cells; every other cell is 0.","x":1820,"y":510,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"0d77b61a83c6b04c","type":"text","text":"**`lidar_labels`**\n\nAt each lidar point: abs_rel = |fitted depth - z| / z.\n\ntarget = 1 where abs_rel > tau (0.1). About 9% of cells hold a lidar point.","x":1820,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"fd2013b570c6b480","type":"text","text":"`feature_0` to `feature_63` (64)\n\nWhat DA2 has worked out about each cell before it commits to a depth.","x":2300,"y":0,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8fddf3365c51b23d","type":"text","text":"`depth` (1)\n\nDA2's own prediction: the scene layout, near against far.","x":2300,"y":170,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"4b181fe746cc2525","type":"text","text":"`temporal_relstd` (1)\n\nHow much DA2's depth of the same 3D point disagrees across frames.","x":2300,"y":340,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6295f08b8342338b","type":"text","text":"`radar_residual` (1)\n\nHow far DA2's depth is from radar's.","x":2300,"y":510,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ce34d6029eca157f","type":"text","text":"`radar_valid` (1)\n\n1 where the residual is a measurement.","x":2300,"y":680,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1a4e1612052226ea","type":"text","text":"`target` `[1, 74, 132]`\n\n1 where DA2's depth is off by more than 10%.","x":2300,"y":900,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"8dff4287fcf364e2","type":"text","text":"`mask` `[1, 74, 132]`\n\n1 where the cell holds a lidar point.","x":2300,"y":1070,"width":340,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"97eb734a8d183a06","type":"text","text":"## ConfidenceHead\n\n`x: [B, 68, 74, 132]`\n\n1. Standardize each channel with the mean and std of the train split\n2. conv 3x3 to 64, ReLU\n3. conv 3x3 to 64, ReLU\n4. conv 3x3 to 32, ReLU\n5. conv 1x1 to 1 logit per cell\n\nThe only part that is trained.","x":2780,"y":0,"width":340,"height":810,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"d3e6528dd7b116a7","type":"text","text":"## p_error\n\n`[B, 1, 74, 132]`\n\nPer grid cell: the probability that DA2's depth is wrong by more than 10%. One cell covers about 12 x 12 image pixels.","x":3240,"y":170,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"dc2bfa11bd9d6b79","type":"text","text":"**Masked BCE loss**\n\nOver the labeled cells only. Positive cells are weighted by negatives / positives.","x":2780,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"8c89c405a4b88867","type":"text","text":"**Training settings**\n\nAdamW, lr 0.001, cosine schedule, weight decay 0.0001\n\n8 epochs, batch 8, seed 0\n\nDev: 10% of the train scenes, picked by the seed","x":3240,"y":900,"width":340,"height":300},
		{"id":"64d8a1923822276c","type":"text","text":">[!tip] Radar Fit\n\nDA2's disparity is only correct up to two unknown numbers per image: a multiplier and an offset. The fit finds them by ordinary least squares over the radar points in that image:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{z} \\approx \\text{scale} \\cdot \\text{disparity} + \\text{shift}$$\n\nEach radar point contributes one pair: DA2's disparity at its pixel and its own $1/z$\n\nWith about 94 points and two unknowns, the fit can only absorb an error the whole image shares, such as a wrong overall scale.\n\nOnce the two numbers are known,\n\n$1 / (\\text{scale} \\cdot \\text{disparity} + \\text{shift})$ gives DA2's depth in meters at any pixel.\n\nIt fails 17% of the time due to:\n- Too few points\n- All points have the same disparity (nothing to fit)\n- Non-positive scale, e.g. fitted slope is zero or negative (due to missing elevation scale in rad)","x":460,"y":1360,"width":1035,"height":500},
		{"id":"cde181f230474bbe","type":"text","text":">[!tip] Lidar Fit\n\nDA2's disparity is only correct up to two unknown numbers per image: a multiplier and an offset. The lidar fit finds them the same way the radar fit does, by ordinary least squares, but over the lidar points in that image:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{z} \\approx \\text{scale} \\cdot \\text{disparity} + \\text{shift}$$\n\nEach lidar point contributes one pair: DA2's disparity at its pixel and its own $1/z$\n\nWith about 3,600 points (the v1.0-mini mean) and two unknowns, the fit can only absorb an error the whole image shares, such as a wrong overall scale.\n\nOnce the two numbers are known,\n\n$1 / (\\text{scale} \\cdot \\text{disparity} + \\text{shift})$ gives DA2's depth in meters at any pixel.\n\nThe lidar fit is used in two places:\n- The labels: abs_rel = |fitted depth - z| / z at each lidar point\n- `temporal_variation`: it lifts each cell to a 3D point before following it into the neighbor frames\n\nIt fails for the same three reasons as the radar fit, but rarely: 0.2% of the v1.0-mini images, all night images where DA2's disparity does not follow the lidar (non-positive scale). An image with no lidar fit has no labels and an all-zero `temporal_relstd`.","x":1535,"y":1360,"width":1035,"height":560}
	],
